{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/993217-the-bane-s-made-me-do-it-or-i-did-it-and-they-came-to-me","id":993217,"title":"The Bane's Made me Do it? or i did it and they came to me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T18:31:15-07:00","id":993217,"title":"The Bane's Made me Do it? or i did it and they came to me","content":"I was thinking about the slashers, i saw someone mention the idea of Spirits influencing people to do horrible things..but is it always the case? do serial killers attract banes. Do they do horrible things and then call the banes, or the banes influence them to do such heinous acts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:38:41-07:00","id":993222,"title":"","content":"Serial killers do horrible things, attract banes that admires their creativity, and become fomori. While some fomori become mass killers after losing enough Autonomy, they are biological machines by that time instead of real people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:55:33-07:00","id":993234,"title":"","content":"Essentially both. There's pretty much no &quot;always&quot; here. Some Banes just hang around horrible people to soak in the evil, and some Banes actively encourage terrible acts by humans. Some do both. Some are up to completely different things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:04:26-07:00","id":993242,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that people must be somehow &quot;tainted&quot; or &quot;spiritually polluted&quot; before Banes can possess them. This is why PENTEX puts out &quot;tainted&quot; products - so people become open to Bane possession. Sometimes the taint is physical such as the old standby of toxic waste &quot;mutating&quot; a person, or strange chemicals being injected or ingested into the person. Sometimes the taint is emotional or mental to put someone in the right frame of mind so that Banes can possess them (I am thinking here of the taint you get from playing certain violent video games or the occult oriented Black Dog games).<br /> <br /> Presumably by their actions, people can taint themselves by violating certain taboos that allow Banes to possess them without this.<br /> <br /> So either case can be correct depending on what the ST wants for that fomori. They might be engaged in tainted actions on their own that opens them up for Bane possession, or they might be innocents who inadvertently were tainted by exposure to something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:03:18-07:00","id":993267,"title":"","content":"It says it clearly in the werewolf Players Guide 2nd edition &quot;The wyrm does NOT force people to do evil&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> that being said, theirs examples to the contrary galore. hither and thither, both happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:07:40-07:00","id":993296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/993217-the-bane-s-made-me-do-it-or-i-did-it-and-they-came-to-me?p=993267#post993267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says it clearly in the werewolf Players Guide 2nd edition &quot;The wyrm does NOT force people to do evil&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> that being said, theirs examples to the contrary galore. hither and thither, both happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further in that quote, Ethan Skemp laid out that the Wyrm, via banes, doesn't need to force humans to do terrible things, because they do that themselves. Also, taint doesn't mean that the devil made you do it, but that you did it, and the devil noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:09:18-07:00","id":993497,"title":"","content":"Yes I remember that but only have a h a rd copy not a PDF of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://im